T15:11:51Z","o":false,"dup":false}],"related":[],"revisions":[{"revision":1,"changed_at":"2026-10-31T00:53:01Z"}],"entities":[{"name":"Melania Trump","kind":"person","mentions":11},{"name":"Ukraine","kind":"place","mentions":7},{"name":"Russia","kind":"place","mentions":6},{"name":"Oleshky","kind":"place","mentions":4},{"name":"White House","kind":"organisation","mentions":4},{"name":"Ukrainian","kind":"place","mentions":3},{"name":"Oleshky","kind":"person","mentions":1},{"name":"Pope Leo","kind":"person","mentions":1},{"name":"Russian","kind":"group","mentions":1},{"name":"Ukrainian","kind":"group","mentions":1}],"disputes":[],"summary":{"text":"First Lady Melania Trump secured a ceasefire in the Ukrainian city of Oleshky on October 23, 2026, mediated by the U.S. Embassy in Russia. Ukraine confirmed this ceasefire, which was aimed at facilitating aid and evacuations. The White House announced that Melania Trump had secured a temporary ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine in the Russian-occupied city of Oleshky.","text_hi":null,"model":"qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:37:35Z"},"context":{"background":[{"title":"2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine","extract":"On 24 February 2022, during the Russo-Ukrainian war, Russia launched a full-scale invasion of Ukraine, starting the current phase of the war, the largest conflict in Europe since World War II. By April 2022, the invasion's initial goal of a rapid Russian victory via decapitation had failed, with Ukraine pushing back the northern arm of the invasion and preventing the capture of Kyiv. Following this, the war transitioned to more conventional fighting in the south and east of Ukraine.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"Russia","extract":"Russia, or the Russian Federation, is a country in Eastern Europe and North Asia. It is the largest country in the world, spanning eleven time zones and sharing land borders with fourteen countries. With a population of over 140 million, Russia is the most populous country in Europe and the ninth-most populous in the world. It is a highly urbanised country, with three-fourths of its population living in urban areas. Moscow, the most populous metropolitan area in Europe, is the capital and largest city of Russia, while Saint Petersburg is its second-largest city and a major cultural centre.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"RU"},{"title":"Ukraine","extract":"Ukraine is a country in Eastern Europe. It is the second-largest country in Europe after Russia, which borders it to the east and northeast. Ukraine also borders Belarus to the north; Poland and Slovakia to the west; Hungary, Romania and Moldova to the southwest; and the Black Sea and the Sea of Azov to the south and southeast. Kyiv is Ukraine's capital and largest city, followed by Kharkiv, Odesa, and Dnipro. The official language is Ukrainian. Ukraine covers about 600,000 km2 (230,000 sq mi), with around 32 million people.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukraine","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"UA"}],"arc":{"reports":214,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T13:02:00Z","first_title":"Democrats explode over Trump’s Russia diesel deal","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxNMVNFSUNjZlhRWFRFVUJEaWJmamxqbnhXMnlvWFVqUWtSVnE0a05fZjROUGV3b3FaSjR1WWtqUFJzN1kyamxRbC10TUVkLXlkM2hNYlhpTXJYWXBFNU5iVmVBRVdDYVdFVmEtalZGeER5X2Rqdm5CQ1MxRVpxRnFVOU8ySzF6QXFSVHl3dUE5WTBhbkZMRmc?oc=5","first_publisher":"The Hill","earlier":[{"id":"e_9db0df2d9103","title":"🇺🇦🇷🇺 Scenes from a RARE CEASEFIRE in Russian-occupied Ukraine Evacuations and aid deliveries unfolded today in Oleshky during a localized truce reportedly brokered by Melania Trump with Pope Leo XIV’s involvement. Humanitarian teams from both","date":"2026-10-31T08:30:00Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/C